    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Corbin Carroll**, who boasts our highest efficiency score at 78.97. Despite a 42% rain risk warning, the matchup against McGreevy (xERA 4.53) provides a prime opportunity for **Corbin Carroll** to leverage his elite speed, our primary focus for category stabilization. Joining him in the \"Strong\" start tier are **Josh Naylor** (65.60) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (64.03). **Tyler Soderstrom** specifically benefits from the wind blowing out, which buoys his projection despite a neutral matchup, while **Josh Naylor** remains our most consistent offensive anchor in the heart of the order.\n\nNavigating the bottom of our lineup required a nuanced look at platoon splits and park factors. **Jose Caballero** (54.92) earned the nod at Utility over other fringe options; despite a subpar spot in the order, his extreme positive platoon split against the opposing southpaw allows him to outperform his base projection. Conversely, **James Wood** (52.59) draws a difficult assignment against S\u00e1nchez, but his elite xwOBA metrics keep him in the lineup despite the tough SP_xERA of 2.84. **Henry Bolte** (52.27) rounds out our top-tier exposure, as his leadoff status provides a massive boost to his run-scoring floor.\n\nThe bench remains largely depleted due to the injury status of **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Giancarlo Stanton**, alongside a lack of scheduled games for **Mickey Moniak** and **Austin Riley**. Within the active group, **Cole Young** (44.97), **Max Muncy** (47.62), and **Zach McKinstry** (48.31) are clearly functioning as our marginal starters. **Zach McKinstry** came closest to being bumped in favor of high-ceiling bench depth, but his park-factor edge against Imai just barely cleared the threshold to keep him in the mix. We are proceeding with caution regarding the weather in the **Corbin Carroll** game and will monitor the lineups for **Seiya Suzuki**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, **Kyle Karros**, **Carson Williams**, and **Travis Bazzana** to ensure no late-breaking advantages emerge for our depth pieces.",
